35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The timing data is clear. A full pass takes over an hour. The management rate is high.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,The calendar shows two people are away most months. The kitchen use is concentrated on three of us.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The chat logs show conflicts start with reminders. The previous tenants stopped speaking by year two.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,The receipts show we buy spray twice a month. The timing confirms it takes a long time.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The grout gets dirty in eleven days. ""Done"" means different things to different people.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, if two people are away, the remaining three carry the load. That is inefficient.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, exactly. And the kitchen mess comes from the same three people. It’s not fair.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Rin, the cost is significant. But the social cost of the previous arrangement was higher.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Victoria, I agree. But I still need to know who pays. The receipts are clear.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, if the grout gets dirty so fast, a weekly clean might not be enough.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, a paid service might handle the grout better. The rate sheet shows it’s feasible.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, but who pays? If we split it, the absent people pay for work they don’t do.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, that is a valid point. We need a system that accounts for absence.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, I think a fixed rota might be better. We can adjust for absences.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I am not sure. I just want it to be clean. I don't want to guess.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I think a fixed weekly rota is the most logical. It is predictable and fair.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I agree. A fixed rota allows us to see who is doing what.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am concerned about the social aspect, but a clear system might help.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I like the idea of a fixed rota. It’s clear and simple.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I think a fixed rota is good. It removes the guesswork.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
